- Deleting a branch or a tag takes the reading of its tip, so a branch which moved since it was
- listed is not deleted by mistake. `makeTag` makes a lightweight tag. `annotatedTag` writes a tag
- object with a message, and optionally a signature.
+ Borrar una rama o una etiqueta recibe la lectura de su punta, así que una rama que se ha movido
+ desde que se listó no se borra por error. `makeTag` crea una etiqueta ligera. `annotatedTag`
+ escribe un objeto etiqueta con un mensaje y, opcionalmente, una firma.

- ### Cloning, fetching and pushing
+ ### Clonar, traer y enviar

- An operation which reaches a remote needs the `Online` capability. It blocks until it is done,
- and reports its progress through a `Git.Activity`: a shared tracker of atomic counters, updated
- as objects arrive, which a user interface may poll from another thread with `report()`.
+ Una operación que llega a un remoto necesita la capacidad `Online`. Se bloquea hasta que termina,
+ e informa de su progreso mediante un `Git.Activity`: un registro compartido de contadores
+ atómicos, actualizado a medida que llegan objetos, que una interfaz de usuario puede consultar
+ desde otro hilo con `report()`.

= as objects arrive, which a user interface may poll from another thread with `report()`.
